Subject: [PATCH] realtek: use the upstream MDIO driver

Switch the realtek subtargets from OpenWrt's own MDIO driver
(mdio-realtek-otto) to the upstream one (mdio-realtek-rtl9300), which
covers all four families since the backports 031-01..34. On top of
those, the kernel carries the four upstream commits it lacked (031-35
to 031-38) and a series for the hardware polling setup that OpenWrt's
driver does and upstream's left to the boot loader (725-01 to 725-06,
on its way to netdev).

The upstream driver binds the RTL839x controller by its fallback
compatible realtek,rtl8391-mdio, which rtl839x.dtsi didn't have.
realtek,otto-mdio stays, as the DSA driver looks the controller up by
it.

OpenWrt's driver is only turned off here: its patch provides Makefile
context for the SerDes and RTL960x MDIO patches.

---
diff --git a/target/linux/realtek/dts/rtl839x.dtsi b/target/linux/realtek/dts/rtl839x.dtsi
index 90f6144..b1a87b8 100644
--- a/target/linux/realtek/dts/rtl839x.dtsi
+++ b/target/linux/realtek/dts/rtl839x.dtsi
@@ -229,7 +229,7 @@
 		};
 
 		mdio_ctrl: mdio-controller {
-			compatible = "realtek,rtl8392-mdio", "realtek,otto-mdio";
+			compatible = "realtek,rtl8392-mdio", "realtek,rtl8391-mdio", "realtek,otto-mdio";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 
diff --git a/target/linux/realtek/rtl838x/config-6.18 b/target/linux/realtek/rtl838x/config-6.18
index 49d382d..377513a 100644
--- a/target/linux/realtek/rtl838x/config-6.18
+++ b/target/linux/realtek/rtl838x/config-6.18
@@ -129,10 +129,10 @@ CONFIG_MDIO_BITBANG=y
 CONFIG_MDIO_BUS=y
 CONFIG_MDIO_GPIO=y
 CONFIG_MDIO_I2C=y
-CONFIG_MDIO_REALTEK_OTTO=y
+# CONFIG_MDIO_REALTEK_OTTO is not set
 CONFIG_MDIO_REALTEK_OTTO_AUX=y
 CONFIG_MDIO_REALTEK_OTTO_SERDES=y
-# CONFIG_MDIO_REALTEK_RTL9300 is not set
+CONFIG_MDIO_REALTEK_RTL9300=y
 CONFIG_MDIO_SMBUS=y
 CONFIG_MFD_CORE=y
 # CONFIG_MFD_HASIVO_STC8 is not set
